{"id": 1924792, "name": "COOKE v. PARIS MOUNTAIN WATER CO.", "name_abbreviation": "Cooke v. Paris Mountain Water Co.", "decision_date": "1909-04-09", "docket_number": "7123", "first_page": "235", "last_page": "236", "citations": [{"type": "official", "cite": "82 S.C. 235"}], "court": {"name_abbreviation": "S.C.", "id": 8894, "name": "Supreme Court of South Carolina"}, "jurisdiction": {"id": 59, "name_long": "South Carolina", "name": "S.C."}, "cites_to": [{"cite": "200 U. S,, 59", "category": "reporters:federal", "reporter": "U.S.", "opinion_index": -1}, {"cite": "36 L. R. A., 535", "category": "reporters:federal", "reporter": "L.R.A.", "opinion_index": -1}, {"cite": "49 L. R. A., 572", "category": "reporters:federal", "reporter": "L.R.A.", "opinion_index": -1}, {"cite": "62 S'. C., 232", "category": "reporters:state", "reporter": "S.C.", "opinion_index": -1}, {"cite": "215 Pa. St., 275", "category": "reporters:state", "reporter": "Pa.", "case_ids": [948444], "opinion_index": -1, "case_paths": ["/pa/215/0275-01"]}, {"cite": "15 L. R. A., 375", "category": "reporters:federal", "reporter": "L.R.A.", "opinion_index": -1}, {"cite": "58 S'. C., 413", "category": "reporters:state", "reporter": "S.C.", "case_ids": [4413448], "opinion_index": -1, "case_paths": ["/sc/58/0413-01"]}, {"cite": "19 S. C., 412", "category": "reporters:state", "reporter": "S.C.", "case_ids": [4379914], "weight": 2, "opinion_index": -1, "case_paths": ["/sc/19/0412-01"]}], "analysis": {"cardinality": 179, "char_count": 2130, "ocr_confidence": 0.596, "pagerank": {"raw": 7.005277023198264e-08, "percentile": 0.4231984181317135}, "sha256": "741fb1c63997acefdc16380b6f2312cb3760ad4dc8dcb23b234e970372bffe4e", "simhash": "1:c7f89cc844bb21bc", "word_count": 378}, "last_updated": "2024-02-27T21:13:54.448445+00:00", "provenance": {"date_added": "2019-08-29", "source": "Harvard", "batch": "2018"}, "casebody": {"judges": [], "parties": ["COOKE v. PARIS MOUNTAIN WATER CO."], "opinions": [{"text": "The opinion of the Court was delivered by\nMr. Justice Woods.\nThis is an appeal from an order overruling a demurrer to the complaint. The contract of the defendant with the city of Greenville is not in the record, while in the very similar case of Ancrum v. Camden Water, Light and Ice Co., post 284, the contract of the water company was set out as a part of the complaint. The complaint in this case, however, rests on the proposition that a contract of a water company with a municipality, containing a general stipulation that it would furnish an adequate supply of water for the extinguishment of fires, carries with such stipulation liability to a private owner of property for fire losses, which would have been prevented if the defendant had not negligently failed to provide water pressure sufficient to extinguish the fire. The case of Ancrum v. Camden Water, Light and Ice Co. holds that the contract does not cover such liability, and that the plaintiff cannot recover.\nThe judgment of the Circuit Court is reversed.", "type": "majority", "author": "Mr. Justice Woods."}], "attorneys": ["Messrs. Cothran, Dean & Cothran, for appellants,", "Mr. J. J. McSwain, contra,"], "corrections": "", "head_matter": "7123\nCOOKE v. PARIS MOUNTAIN WATER CO.\nDamages \u2014 Towns and Cities \u2014 Wateb Company. \u2014 The provision in a contract between a water supply company and a municipality that it would furnish an adequate supply of water for the extinguishment of fires does not carry liability to a private owner of property for losses which would have been prevented if the defendant had not negligently failed to provide water pressure sufficient to extinguish the fire.\nBefore Keugi-i, J., Greenville, March, 1908.\nReversed.\nAction by C. E. Cooke against Paris Mountain Water Company and American Pipe Manufacturing Company. Erom order overruling demurrer, defendants appeal.\nMessrs. Cothran, Dean & Cothran, for appellants,\ncite: 19 S. C., 412; 58 S'. C., 413; 30' Ency., 430-, and cases cited in note; 15 L. R. A., 375; 1 Farnham on Waters, 842-8; 6 E. R. A. (N. S.), 429; 33 E. R. A., 59; 215 Pa. St., 275.\nMr. J. J. McSwain, contra,\ncites: 29 Cyc., 426; 20 Cyc., 1159, 1160'; 62 S'. C., 232 ; 49 L. R. A., 572; 36 L. R. A., 535; 19 S'. C., 412; 46 E. R. A., 514; 6 R. R. \u00c1. (N. S.), 1171; 200 U. S,, 59.\nApril 9, 1909."}, "file_name": "0235-01", "first_page_order": 247, "last_page_order": 248}